Ciphey's binaries include data from its dependencies. That data and its sources:

gibberish-or-not (https://github.com/bee-san/gibberish-or-not, MIT License)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Its English language pack (languages/en/model.bin) holds letter n-gram counts and a word
list derived from these sources; no text of the sources is included:
- Project Gutenberg books (https://www.gutenberg.org): public domain in the USA.
- Tatoeba English sentences (https://tatoeba.org), export of 2026-10-31: CC BY 2.0 FR,
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/fr/, by the Tatoeba contributors
  (https://tatoeba.org/en/users/all).
- Moby Word Lists by Grady Ward (Project Gutenberg ebook 3201): public domain.
gibberish-or-not's NOTICE has the details.
